		(uuid "bdd1b237-8b21-493f-82c7-85c212307bc0")
	)
	(text "- Thermistor is for inrush current limiting\n- May not be needed for some/most DC power supplies.\n- Should be rated for at least 5A with a low hot resistance.\n- Replace TH1 with a >6A Schottky diode for reverse protection."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.526 57.658 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cbc7ed8e-cbd8-4e9f-80d3-3c2434f7550d")
	)
	(text "- 10µF capacitors outside of the RF section can be X5R or X7R.\n- 10µF is the capacitance at 0V, under 10µF with voltage applied is acceptable.\n- In order to reduce ringing, place the gate driver output as close to the gate as possible.\n- Oscillator frequency should be within ±5KHz of 470KHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 70.104 175.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d2c9bd32-6b9b-4e4d-859d-645b496e4d5a")
	)
